<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 18 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 18 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said on Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 18 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Auburn, Ala., $11 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Pinellas Co., Fla., $83.11 million revenue bonds (MBIA alternate bidding program.)</p>
<p>--Laurens-Marathon School District, Iowa, $1.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Laurel, Miss., $4.000 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cohasset, Mass., $4.515 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Plymouth, Mich., $7.355 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Lumberton Township, N.J., $4.029 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Clark County, Nev., $97.91 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Lyme Central School District, N.Y., $1.595 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Massapequa Park, N.Y., $1.572 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Southern Cayuga Central School District, N.Y., $4.21 million school bonds.</p>
</text>
